cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If this code is useful to you, please cite this repository."
type: software
title: "Optical Music Recognition for Orchestral Full Scores with Varying Staff Layouts"
abstract: >-
  A pipeline-based OMR system for orchestral full scores. An MLLM combined with OCR parses the page
  layout and per-staff instrument metadata; a segmentation-based OMR backbone uses that metadata to
  assemble a multi-instrument symbolic score, handling a staff count that varies from system to
  system.
repository-code: "https://github.com/boyuan-ch/omr-varying-staff"
license: MIT
year: 2026
authors:
  - alias: "boyuan-ch"
references:
  - type: data
    title: "The Nine Symphonies of Beethoven: A Digital Edition"
    year: 2009
    publisher:
      name: "Center for Computer Assisted Research in the Humanities (CCARH), Stanford University"
    url: "https://www.ccarh.org/publications/beethoven-symphonies/"
    notes: >-
      Source of the symbolic ground truth this project evaluates against, via the MuseData format.
      Not redistributed here; see data/README.md.
